<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ahmed al-Sharaa</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Abu Mohammad al-Julani</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ahmed al-Sharaa, earlier known as Abu Mohammad al-Julani, is a Syrian militant leader and politician. As head of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hayat-tahrir-al-sham">Hayat Tahrir al-Sham</a> in Idlib he led the offensive that overthrew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bashar-al-assad">Bashar al-Assad</a> in December 2024, ending more than five decades of Assad family rule, and he was named president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>'s transitional government in January 2025.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ahmed-al-sharaa.jpg" alt="Ahmed al-Sharaa" width="320" height="429" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original photo by Foreign, Commonwealth &amp;amp; Development Office, used under CC BY 4.0. Cropped by HurricaneEdgar. · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ahmed_al-Sharaa,_President_of_Syria,_in_March_2026.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
